[{:db/id 17592186096630 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d990e769-49e8-553e-999b-5b9c5313abd0" "question-4060660e-a98e-5a45-8a1f-74d923cbf4d9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096631 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bacd6074-8287-5758-9454-33c120a66361" "question-5b26923d-aa9d-5c1e-919b-9d716067cb9d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096632 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-92db8444-ee84-5a2b-a100-391911e28dfc" "question-368aa1bb-68dd-5e11-83de-3c6725fca7d6" "question-9831af65-2b7f-5270-b7a1-fe24be0274fd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096633 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d31b1ab6-50b9-57eb-ba32-5357e77d62ee" "question-d07197e2-a19c-5121-ad34-53964d711400" "question-174ba687-7b9b-5ccb-9e0f-e16e772aa04c" "question-e24c9c25-519c-53c3-84e2-e60c0348d7f8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d990e769-49e8-553e-999b-5b9c5313abd0" :question/id #uuid "d990e769-49e8-553e-999b-5b9c5313abd0" :question/math-academy-id "q-346165" :question/problem "![](images/29/29729a2b35aa370f46f15d221764b3cf8fd6344ff475016b92a974cfb31b08c2.png)\n\nFor the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+1$ shown above, what is the expression for the area $A$ as a definite integral?\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $A$ | $=$ | $\\int $ | {{field-2}} | $\\text{d}x$ |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We want to express the area $A$ between the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+1$ and the $x$-axis, between $x=0$ and $x=3.$\n\nThis can be expressed as the definite integral of $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+1$ between the lower limit $x=0$ and the upper limit $x=3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+1\\,\\text{d}x\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ca90be99-490d-506f-9fbe-c995ce3a66ab" "answer-field-6ec4d0af-543d-5963-b3ad-9fc1ce6b0e91" "answer-fi