ef106b1e7d8.png)\n\nFor the function $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}+1$ shown above, what is the expression for the area $A$ as a definite integral?\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $A$ | $=$ | $\\int $ | {{field-2}} | $\\text{d}x$ |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We want to express the area $A$ between the function $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}+1$ and the $x$-axis, between $x=1$ and $x=2.$\n\nThis can be expressed as the definite integral of $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}+1$ between the lower limit $x=1$ and the upper limit $x=2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{x}+1\\,\\text{d}x\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a5b98d43-6d7f-5c4b-8935-2e136fb34202" "answer-field-f123d4f1-c3ab-5a09-8eef-7519f7b35fbb" "answer-field-1b59a680-1968-57e4-bebd-d8584cb79a8b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a5b98d43-6d7f-5c4b-8935-2e136fb34202" :answer-field/id #uuid "a5b98d43-6d7f-5c4b-8935-2e136fb34202" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-190cbe45-4bb3-5cf4-a35e-c9953f59cc89" :answer-field/choices ["answer-190cbe45-4bb3-5cf4-a35e-c9953f59cc89"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-190cbe45-4bb3-5cf4-a35e-c9953f59cc89" :answer/id #uuid "190cbe45-4bb3-5cf4-a35e-c9953f59cc89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f123d4f1-c3ab-5a09-8eef-7519f7b35fbb" :answer-field/id #uuid "f123d4f1-c3ab-5a09-8eef-7519f7b35fbb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1d55cde1-0ef0-50b5-87b3-6f37123ec4a7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1d55cde1-0ef0-50b5-87b3-6f37123ec4a7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d55cde1-0ef0-50b5-87b3-6f37123ec4a7" :answer/id #uuid "1d55cde1-0ef0-50b5-87b3-6f37123ec4a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{x}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1b59a680-1968-57e4-bebd-d8584cb79a8b" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b59a680-1968-57e4-bebd-d8584cb79a8b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-3d44457a-5400-5106-a195-e87183c76d4f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3d44457a-5400-5106-a195-e87183c76d4f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d44457a-5400-5106-a195-e87183c76d4f" :answer/id #uuid "3d44457a-5400-5106-a195-e87183c76d4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bacd6074-8287-5758-9454-33c120a66361" :question/id #uuid "bacd6074-8287-5758-9454-33c120a66361" :question/math-academy-id "q-346173" :question/problem "Express ${\\int }_{1}^{5}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+2)\\,\\text{d}x$ as the limit of a left Riemann sum.\n\n*Hint: Write down the missing expression in terms of $i$ and $n.$*\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{5}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+2)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡($\n{{field-1}}\n$)+2)\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]$" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+2)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+2,$ the lower bound is $a=1,$ and the upper bound is $b=5.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{5-1}{n}=\\frac{4}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{5}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+2)\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(1+i\\cdot \\frac{4}{n})\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(1+\\frac{4i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\,1+\\frac{4i}{n}\\,)+2)\\,\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f2252516-11cb-503e-94e5-fbb51ee360c4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f2252516-11cb-503e-94e5-fbb51ee360c4" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2252516-11cb-503e-94e5-fbb51ee360c4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2c9696ed-0cf7-51a5-ab03-f99476ed2805" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2c9696ed-0cf7-51a5-ab03-f99476ed2805"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c9696ed-0cf7-51a5-ab03-f99476ed2805" :answer/id #uuid "2c9696ed-0cf7-51a5-ab03-f99476ed2805" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\frac{4i}{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233960 :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{10}{x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)={x}^{1/2},$ the lower bound is $a=1,$ and the upper bound is $b=10.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{10-1}{n}=\\frac{9}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{10}{x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(1+i\\cdot \\frac{9}{n})\\cdot \\frac{9}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(1+\\frac{9i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{9}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(\\,1+\\frac{9i}{n}\\,)}^{\\,1/2}\\,\\cdot \\frac{9}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-5b26923d-aa9d-5c1e-919b-9d716067cb9d" :question/id #uuid "5b26923d-aa9d-5c1e-919b-9d716067cb9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-113883" :question/problem "What is ${\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)={x}^{4},$ the lower bound is $a=1,$ and the upper bound is $b=2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{2-1}{n}=\\frac{1}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(1+i\\cdot \\frac{1}{n})\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(1+\\frac{i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(1+\\frac{i}{n})}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f3299ff3-e06a-576d-9e6b-49153eef928c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f3299ff3-e06a-576d-9e6b-49153eef928c" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3299ff3-e06a-576d-9e6b-49153eef928c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9ddf0c06-3e13-5114-ae8a-765ff61402f7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9ddf0c06-3e13-5114-ae8a-765ff61402f7" "answer-947fa02e-9a14-57a5-985e-c7e642d3bff6" "answer-ea0a3613-4a32-5b89-8a35-66e90173d741" "answer-3773932e-fae8-57ab-a030-de021b53748f" "answer-f561ae55-84c0-546c-9312-d11812ce786d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ddf0c06-3e13-5114-ae8a-765ff61402f7" :answer/id #uuid "9ddf0c06-3e13-5114-ae8a-765ff61402f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(1+\\frac{i}{n})}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-947fa02e-9a14-57a5-985e-c7e642d3bff6" :answer/id #uuid "947fa02e-9a14-57a5-985e-c7e642d3bff6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(1+\\frac{i}{n})}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea0a3613-4a32-5b89-8a35-66e90173d741" :answer/id #uuid "ea0a3613-4a32-5b89-8a35-66e90173d741" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(1+\\frac{i}{n})}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3773932e-fae8-57ab-a030-de021b53748f" :answer/id #uuid "3773932e-fae8-57ab-a030-de021b53748f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(2+\\frac{i}{n})}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f561ae55-84c0-546c-9312-d11812ce786d" :answer/id #uuid "f561ae55-84c0-546c-9312-d11812ce786d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(2+\\frac{i}{n})}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-92db8444-ee84-5a2b-a100-391911e28dfc" :question/id #uuid "92db8444-ee84-5a2b-a100-391911e28dfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-346192" :question/problem "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[7{(1+\\frac{2k}{n})}^{-3}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}].\n$$\n\n$\\,f(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and \n$\\,b=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=1.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{2}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{n}=\\frac{b-1}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nConsequently, ${x}_{k}=1+\\frac{2k}{n}$ and $f({x}_{k})=7{x}_{k}^{-3}.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}7{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[7{(1+\\frac{2k}{n})}^{-3}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \n\n$$\nf(x)=7{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{and}\\,b=3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a295c97d-d2d9-5a3d-9891-87fc0cfd77f6" "answer-field-02fa8ffe-84d7-5a81-9584-e9e83fe39768"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a295c97d-d2d9-5a3d-9891-87fc0cfd77f6" :answer-field/id #uuid "a295c97d-d2d9-5a3d-9891-87fc0cfd77f6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e9b4387d-0850-5ada-aa3a-96062914b732" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e9b4387d-0850-5ada-aa3a-96062914b732"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9b4387d-0850-5ada-aa3a-96062914b732" :answer/id #uuid "e9b4387d-0850-5ada-aa3a-96062914b732" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7x^{-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-02fa8ffe-84d7-5a81-9584-e9e83fe39768" :answer-field/id #uuid "02fa8ffe-84d7-5a81-9584-e9e83fe39768" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-80e91b06-f9f7-58e7-9b93-fa4bf08254ae" :answer-field/choices ["answer-80e91b06-f9f7-58e7-9b93-fa4bf08254ae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80e91b06-f9f7-58e7-9b93-fa4bf08254ae" :answer/id #uuid "80e91b06-f9f7-58e7-9b93-fa4bf08254ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-368aa1bb-68dd-5e11-83de-3c6725fca7d6" :question/id #uuid "368aa1bb-68dd-5e11-83de-3c6725fca7d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-346198" :question/problem "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[{log}_{2}\\,(5(3+\\frac{4k}{n}))\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}].\n$$\n\n$\\,f(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and \n$\\,b=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=3.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{4}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{n}=\\frac{b-3}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=7.\n$$\n\nConsequently, ${x}_{k}=3+\\frac{4k}{n}$ and $f({x}_{k})={log}_{2}\\,(5{x}_{k}).$ By replacing the sample point ${x}_{k}$ with the variable $x,$ we find the original function.\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{7}{log}_{2}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[{log}_{2}\\,(5(3+\\frac{4k}{n}))\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \n\n$$\nf(x)={log}_{2}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{and}\\,b=7.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1ce33564-9610-5802-9f60-271794918cb3" "answer-field-3d2f8892-a963-5ac4-967b-d51cd720e5b7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1ce33564-9610-5802-9f60-271794918cb3" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ce33564-9610-5802-9f60-271794918cb3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-07485527-04b3-57d3-a577-5a960471513a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-07485527-04b3-57d3-a577-5a960471513a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07485527-04b3-57d3-a577-5a960471513a" :answer/id #uuid "07485527-04b3-57d3-a577-5a960471513a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\log_2(5x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3d2f8892-a963-5ac4-967b-d51cd720e5b7" :answer-field/id #uuid "3d2f8892-a963-5ac4-967b-d51cd720e5b7" :answer-field/